note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note x25519.om: X25519 (RFC 7748 section 5) for the om/tls TLS 1.3 client (RFC 8446 section 7.4.2).
note Library unit (module code XC): functions and consts only, no om2 line, no main, no globals.
note
note API
note   x25519_scalarmult o edit uchar * k view uchar * u view uchar * to ulong
note     o = X25519(k, u). o, k, u must each be exactly 32 bytes. Returns 0 ok, 1 when the output is
note     all zero (RFC 7748 section 6.1, RFC 8446 section 7.4.2: the caller must abort), 2 when a
note     length is not 32 (nothing is written then). The zero test is computed without branches.
note   x25519_base o edit uchar * k view uchar * to ulong
note     o = X25519(k, 9), same return codes.
note
note Field GF(p), p = 2^255 - 19: ten limbs h0..h9 in ulong cells, radix 2^25.5 (ref10 layout):
note limb i has weight 2^e(i), e(i) = ceil(51 i / 2) = 0 26 51 77 102 128 153 179 204 230, and width
note w(i) = 26 for even i, 25 for odd i (e(10) = 255). A product h_i g_j lands at weight
note e(i) + e(j) = e(i + j) + [i and j odd], and weight 2^255 folds as 19, so column k of a product
note collects coef(i, j) h_i g_j over i + j = k (mod 10) with coef = (1 + [i, j odd]) (19 if i + j >= 10).
note
note Limb bounds (no ulong ever wraps). "Carried" means every limb < 2^26 and limbs 2..9 within their
note width; only limb 1 may exceed 2^25, by at most 91314 (below).
note   decode (fload): limbs within width (top bit of u masked), so carried.
note   mul / mul24 / canonical outputs: carried (fcarry, below).
note   fadd of two carried values: limbs < 2^27.
note   fsub a b = a + 2p - b limbwise, b carried: 2p limbs are 134217690 (i = 0), 67108862 (odd),
note     134217726 (even) and every carried b limb is at or below them (limb 1 <= 33645746 <= 67108862),
note     so no limb wraps; result limbs < 2^26 + 2^27 = 3 * 2^26 = L.
note   fmul inputs: every call site passes carried, fadd or fsub values, so all limbs < L. The largest
note     column coefficient sum is 267 (column 0), so a column is < 267 L^2 < 2^63.24; a carry into the
note     next column is < 2^38.24, so the sum stays below 2^64.
note   fcarry: limbs 0..8 carry into the next limb (shift by the width), limb 9 carries (times 19) into
note     limb 0, then limb 0 carries once more into limb 1: the folded carry is < 19 * 2^38.24, so the
note     second carry out of limb 0 is <= 91315 and limb 1 ends <= 2^25 - 1 + 91315 = 33645746 < 2^26.
note   fmul24: limbs < L times 121665 < 2^44.48, then fcarry.
note   canonical (fstore): the value h < 2^255 - 1 + 91315 * 2^26 < 2p, so q = floor((h + 19) / 2^255)
note     is 0 or 1 and h - q p is the canonical residue (computed with masks only).
note Checked with the Wolfram Language evaluator (2026-10-26):
note   e[i_]:=Ceiling[51 i/2]; coef[i_,j_]:=(1+BitAnd[i,j,1]) If[i+j>=10,19,1];
note   colsum=Table[Total[Flatten@Table[If[Mod[i+j,10]==k,coef[i,j],0],{i,0,9},{j,0,9}]],{k,0,9}];
note   L=3*2^26; col=Max[colsum] L^2; cin=Floor[(col+2^40)/2^25]; c9=Floor[(col+cin)/2^25];
note   c0=Floor[(2^26-1+19 c9)/2^26]; ... ->
note   e[10]=255; widths {26,25,...}; weight identity e[i]+e[j]==e[Mod[i+j,10]]+255[i+j>=10]+[i,j odd]
note   True for all i,j; colsum={267,154,213,118,159,82,105,46,51,10}; Log2[col]=63.2306;
note   col+cin<2^64 True; Log2[c9]=38.2306; c0=91315; t1=33645746 <= 2(2^25-1) True;
note   Sum[pl_i 2^e[i]]==2^255-19 True; 2p limbs {134217690,67108862,134217726,...};
note   hmax<2p True; Log2[3 2^26 121665]=44.4775; (486662-2)/4=121665; PrimeQ[2^255-19] True.
note
note Constant time: no branch, loop count or array index depends on k, u or any intermediate value.
note Every loop has a fixed count; indices depend only on loop counters and slot offsets. The ladder
note swap is an xor with a mask m = 0 - bit; the final reduction subtracts q p with q from a carry
note chain; the all-zero test is ((a | -a) >> 63) ^ 1. Secret arrays (clamped scalar, workspace,
note multiplication scratch) are overwritten with 0 before return. Caveats: omc emits plain AArch64
note and we rely on MUL, ADD, SUB, EOR, AND, ORR, LSL/LSR with register amounts being data-independent
note (no DIT bit is set); register and spill contents are not scrubbed; the length check (return 2)
note branches on public lengths; bounds checks on indices branch on public offsets only.

note workspace slots (ulong offsets into w, 10 limbs each); the inversion reuses the step temporaries
const XCWN ulong 140
const XCX1 ulong 0
const XCX2 ulong 10
const XCZ2 ulong 20
const XCX3 ulong 30
const XCZ3 ulong 40
const XCTA ulong 50
const XCAA ulong 60
const XCTB ulong 70
const XCBB ulong 80
const XCTE ulong 90
const XCTC ulong 100
const XCTD ulong 110
const XCDA ulong 120
const XCCB ulong 130
note a24 = (486662 - 2) / 4 (RFC 7748 section 5)
const XCA24 ulong 121665

note one carry pass: limbs 0..8 into the next limb, limb 9 (times 19) into limb 0, limb 0 into limb 1
fn x25519_fcarry t edit ulong 10 to void
for i ulong 9 unroll
put t add i 1 add get t add i 1 shr get t i sub 26 and i 1
put t i and get t i sub 67108863 mul 33554432 and i 1
end
c = shr get t 9 25
put t 9 and get t 9 33554431
put t 0 add get t 0 mul c 19
c = shr get t 0 26
put t 0 and get t 0 67108863
put t 1 add get t 1 c
end

note slot o = slot a * slot b mod p, carried (o may equal a or b)
fn x25519_fmul w edit ulong XCWN o ulong a ulong b ulong to void
x = new ulong 10 0
y = new ulong 10 0
t = new ulong 10 0
for i ulong 10 unroll
put x i get w add a i
put y i get w add b i
end
for i ulong 10 unroll
for j ulong 10 unroll
put t rem add i j 10 add get t rem add i j 10 mul mul get x i get y j mul add 1 and and i j 1 add 1 mul 18 div add i j 10
end
end
x25519_fcarry t
for i ulong 10 unroll
put w add o i get t i
put x i 0
put y i 0
put t i 0
end
end

note slot o = slot a + slot b limbwise, no carry
fn x25519_fadd w edit ulong XCWN o ulong a ulong b ulong to void
for i ulong 10 unroll
put w add o i add get w add a i get w add b i
end
end

note slot o = slot a + 2p - slot b limbwise, no carry (b must be carried)
fn x25519_fsub w edit ulong XCWN o ulong a ulong b ulong to void
for i ulong 10 unroll
put w add o i sub add get w add a i sub sub 134217726 mul 67108864 and i 1 mul 36 div sub 10 i 10 get w add b i
end
end

note slot o = a24 * slot a, carried
fn x25519_fmul24 w edit ulong XCWN o ulong a ulong to void
t = new ulong 10 0
for i ulong 10 unroll
put t i mul get w add a i XCA24
end
x25519_fcarry t
for i ulong 10 unroll
put w add o i get t i
put t i 0
end
end

note slot o = slot a ^ (2^n), n >= 1 (n public)
fn x25519_fsqn w edit ulong XCWN o ulong a ulong n ulong to void
x25519_fmul w o a a
for i ulong sub n 1
x25519_fmul w o o o
end
end

note slot o = slot a ^ (p - 2) = 1 / a (0 for a = 0), p - 2 = 2^255 - 21: the fixed ref10 chain
note z^11, z^(2^250 - 1), then (2^250 - 1) * 2^5 + 11 = 2^255 - 21. Uses XCTA XCAA XCTB XCBB XCTE;
note o and a must be other slots.
fn x25519_finv w edit ulong XCWN o ulong a ulong to void
x25519_fmul w XCTA a a
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCTA XCTA
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCAA XCAA
x25519_fmul w XCAA a XCAA
x25519_fmul w XCBB XCTA XCAA
x25519_fmul w XCTA XCBB XCBB
x25519_fmul w XCTA XCAA XCTA
x25519_fsqn w XCAA XCTA 5
x25519_fmul w XCTA XCAA XCTA
x25519_fsqn w XCAA XCTA 10
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCAA XCTA
x25519_fsqn w XCTB XCAA 20
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCTB XCAA
x25519_fsqn w XCAA XCAA 10
x25519_fmul w XCTA XCAA XCTA
x25519_fsqn w XCAA XCTA 50
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCAA XCTA
x25519_fsqn w XCTB XCAA 100
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCTB XCAA
x25519_fsqn w XCAA XCAA 50
x25519_fmul w XCTE XCAA XCTA
x25519_fsqn w XCTE XCTE 5
x25519_fmul w o XCTE XCBB
end

note swap slots a and b when m is all ones, keep them when m is 0 (m = 0 - bit, no branch)
fn x25519_fcswap w edit ulong XCWN a ulong b ulong m ulong to void
for i ulong 10 unroll
x = get w add a i
y = get w add b i
d = and m xor x y
put w add a i xor x d
put w add b i xor y d
end
end

note slot o = the 32 little-endian bytes of u with bit 255 masked (RFC 7748 decodeUCoordinate);
note values p..2^255-1 are kept and reduced by the arithmetic. len u = 32 is checked by the caller.
fn x25519_fload w edit ulong XCWN o ulong u view uchar * to void
for i ulong 10
e = div add mul i 51 1 2
b = shr e 3
v = ulong get u b
v = or v shl ulong get u add b 1 8
v = or v shl ulong get u add b 2 16
v = or v shl ulong get u add b 3 24
m = sub shl ulong 1 sub 26 and i 1 1
put w add o i and shr v and e 7 m
end
end

note o = the 32-byte little-endian encoding of the canonical limbs t; returns 1 when o is all zero,
note else 0 (no branch on the value: z = ((a | -a) >> 63) ^ 1 over the OR of the four words)
fn x25519_fenc t view ulong 10 o edit uchar * to ulong
q = new ulong 4 0
for i ulong 10
e = div add mul i 51 1 2
d = shr e 6
s = and e 63
v = get t i
put q d or get q d shl v s
if gt add s sub 26 and i 1 64
d = add d 1
put q d or get q d shr v sub 64 s
end
end
for j ulong 32
v = shr get q shr j 3 mul and j 7 8
put o j uchar and v 255
end
z = or or get q 0 get q 1 or get q 2 get q 3
z = xor shr or z sub 0 z 63 1
for i ulong 4 unroll
put q i 0
end
ret z
end

note o = the canonical 32-byte encoding of slot a (carried input): q = floor((h + 19) / 2^255) by a
note carry chain, then h + 19 q with the carry out of bit 255 dropped = h - q p. Returns x25519_fenc.
fn x25519_fstore w edit ulong XCWN a ulong o edit uchar * to ulong
t = new ulong 10 0
for i ulong 10 unroll
put t i get w add a i
end
c = ulong 19
for i ulong 10 unroll
c = shr add get t i c sub 26 and i 1
end
put t 0 add get t 0 mul c 19
for i ulong 9 unroll
put t add i 1 add get t add i 1 shr get t i sub 26 and i 1
put t i and get t i sub 67108863 mul 33554432 and i 1
end
put t 9 and get t 9 33554431
z = x25519_fenc t o
for i ulong 10 unroll
put t i 0
end
ret z
end

note one Montgomery ladder step (RFC 7748 section 5):
note A = x2 + z2, AA = A^2, B = x2 - z2, BB = B^2, E = AA - BB, C = x3 + z3, D = x3 - z3,
note DA = D A, CB = C B, x3 = (DA + CB)^2, z3 = x1 (DA - CB)^2, x2 = AA BB, z2 = E (AA + a24 E)
fn x25519_step w edit ulong XCWN to void
x25519_fadd w XCTA XCX2 XCZ2
x25519_fmul w XCAA XCTA XCTA
x25519_fsub w XCTB XCX2 XCZ2
x25519_fmul w XCBB XCTB XCTB
x25519_fsub w XCTE XCAA XCBB
x25519_fadd w XCTC XCX3 XCZ3
x25519_fsub w XCTD XCX3 XCZ3
x25519_fmul w XCDA XCTD XCTA
x25519_fmul w XCCB XCTC XCTB
x25519_fadd w XCTA XCDA XCCB
x25519_fmul w XCX3 XCTA XCTA
x25519_fsub w XCTB XCDA XCCB
x25519_fmul w XCTB XCTB XCTB
x25519_fmul w XCZ3 XCX1 XCTB
x25519_fmul w XCX2 XCAA XCBB
x25519_fmul24 w XCTC XCTE
x25519_fadd w XCTC XCAA XCTC
x25519_fmul w XCZ2 XCTE XCTC
end

note the ladder over bits 254..0 of the clamped scalar e, conditional swaps by masks
fn x25519_ladder w edit ulong XCWN e view uchar 32 to void
sw = ulong 0
for i ulong 255
t = sub 254 i
b = and shr ulong get e shr t 3 and t 7 1
sw = xor sw b
m = sub 0 sw
x25519_fcswap w XCX2 XCX3 m
x25519_fcswap w XCZ2 XCZ3 m
sw = b
x25519_step w
end
m = sub 0 sw
x25519_fcswap w XCX2 XCX3 m
x25519_fcswap w XCZ2 XCZ3 m
end

fn x25519_scalarmult o edit uchar * k view uchar * u view uchar * to ulong
if or or ne len o 32 ne len k 32 ne len u 32
ret 2
end
w = new ulong XCWN 0
e = new uchar 32 0
for i ulong 32
put e i get k i
end
put e 0 and get e 0 248
put e 31 or and get e 31 127 64
x25519_fload w XCX1 u
for i ulong 10 unroll
put w add XCX3 i get w add XCX1 i
end
put w XCX2 1
put w XCZ3 1
x25519_ladder w e
x25519_finv w XCTC XCZ2
x25519_fmul w XCX2 XCX2 XCTC
r = x25519_fstore w XCX2 o
for i ulong XCWN
put w i 0
end
for i ulong 32
put e i 0
end
ret r
end

fn x25519_base o edit uchar * k view uchar * to ulong
b = new uchar 32 0
put b 0 9
ret x25519_scalarmult o k b
end
